ath9k: full 5 GHz channel grid 36-177 (adds 68-96, 144, 169-177)

ath9k_5ghz_chantable predates channel 144 and was never extended, so an
AR9344 lists 36-140 and 149-165 and nothing else, whatever the regdb
allows (US already permits 5470-5730 and 5850-5895). Nothing in the
driver limits the frequency: ar9003_hw_set_channel takes any synth
centre >= 4800 MHz, the EEPROM encodes piers as 4800 + 5n, and the
target-power interpolation clamps past the last pier (5825 on the
CPE510). This adds every 20 MHz-spaced channel from 36 to 177 -- the
5340-5480 gap (68-96), 144 (5720) and 169/173/177 (5845-5885) -- so the
mabur relay can follow its peers anywhere in [36, 177]. hw_value is an
index into ah->channels[], so the 5 GHz entries are renumbered and
ATH9K_NUM_CHANNELS grows 38 -> 50 (14 x 2 GHz + 36 x 5 GHz). Which
channels may be used stays the regdb's call (regdb/db.txt, iw reg set).
mabur-openwrt CPE510 (AR9344) firmware.

